der-covers (0.77) and interaction model did not improve on the simple EB-IRT\",\n    \"selection is ignorable for likelihood under searchers that use only observed outcomes\"\n  ],\n  \"queries\": [\n    {\n      \"query\": \"winner's curse selection bias reported score after selecting best configuration among many\",\n      \"category\": \"core_method\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Central problem: the best-of-K searched config scored on the same questions is upward biased (naive signed bias +0.037 in the run).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"adaptive data analysis statistical validity reuse of holdout\",\n      \"category\": \"baseline_comparator\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Adaptive reuse of one question set for selection and scoring; grounds the validity argument (Dwork et al. line).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"Ladder mechanism reliable leaderboard adaptive submissions\",\n      \"category\": \"baseline_comparator\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reporting-mechanism comparator for repeated adaptive evaluation on a shared test set.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"inference on winners selected parameter confidence intervals\",\n      \"category\": \"baseline_comparator\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Econometric post-selection inference for selected best candidates; the run's Bonferroni/resample baselines belong to this neighborhood.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"valid post-selection inference confidence intervals\",\n      \"category\": \"baseline_comparator\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Classical post-selection inference literature; context for simultaneous/Bonferroni-style intervals compared against.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"empirical Bayes shrinkage for selected maximum item response theory LLM benchmark evaluation\",\n@Article{Dwork2014PreservingSV,\n booktitle = {Symposium on the Theory of Computing},\n title = {Preserving Statistical Validity in Adaptive Data Analysis},\n@Article{Dwork2015TheRH,\n booktitle = {Science},\n title = {The reusable holdout: Preserving validity in adaptive data analysis},\n@Article{Dwork2015GeneralizationIA,\n booktitle = {Neural Information Processing Systems},\n title = {Generalization in Adaptive Data Analysis and Holdout Reuse},\n@Article{Feldman2017CalibratingNT,\n booktitle = {Annual Conference Computational Learning Theory},\n title = {Calibrating Noise to Variance in Adaptive Data Analysis},\n@Article{Dwork2017GuiltfreeDR,\n booktitle = {Communications of the ACM},\n title = {Guilt-free data reuse},\n@Article{Marchant2024AdaptiveDA,\n booktitle = {Neural Information Processing Systems},\n title = {Adaptive Data Analysis for Growing Data},\n@Article{Ullman2017TechnicalPB,\n booktitle = {Communications of the ACM},\n title = {Technical Perspective: Building a safety net for data reuse},\n@Article{Wang2024MMLUPro,\n title = {MMLU-Pro: A More Robust and Challenging Multi-Task Language Understanding Benchmark},\n@Article{Khattab2023DSPy,\n title = {DSPy: Compiling Declarative Language Model Calls into Self-Improving Pipelines},\n@Article{OpsahlOng2024MIPRO,\n title = {Optimizing Instructions and Demonstrations for Multi-Stage Language Model Programs},\n@Article{Polo2024EfficientMultiPrompt,\n title = {Efficient multi-prompt evaluation of LLMs},\n@Article{Shi2024PromptBAI,\n title = {Efficient Prompt Optimization Through the Lens of Best Arm Identification},\n@Article{Sclar2023Quantifying,\n title = {Quantifying Language Models' Sensitivity to Spurious Features in Prompt Design or: How I learned to start worrying about prompt formatting},\n@Article{Blum2015Ladder,\n title = {The Ladder: A Reliable Leaderboard for Machine Learning Competitions},\n@Article{Chernozhukov2013Gaussian,\n title = {Gaussian approximations and multiplier bootstrap for maxima of sums of high-dimensional random vectors},\n@Article{Jamieson2016SuccessiveHalving,\n title = {Non-stochastic Best Arm Identification and Hyperparameter Optimization},\n@Article{Recht2019ImageNet,\n title = {Do ImageNet Cla