{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwKdgujn2kxubu3kaeAD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EQDemGvz3oQhc2vEg5e3qB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('reference_query_plan.json'))\nq=[\n(\"Rasch model item response theory logistic latent ability item difficulty\",\"core_method\",\"Gap method-irt-model-background (high): the Bernoulli(sigma(a_k - b_q)) model behind EB-IRT has no IRT/Rasch lineage cited; this credits the foundations. No IRT or Rasch work is in the current bibliography.\"),\n(\"hierarchical Bayesian item response model empirical Bayes marginal maximum likelihood Laplace approximation\",\"core_method\",\"Gap method-irt-model-background (high): ties the hierarchical-prior, Laplace-based empirical-Bayes fitting of EB-IRT to prior IRT estimation work. Distinct from the existing Efron empirical-Bayes entries (Tweedie, Stein), which cover shrinkage and selection bias but not IRT fitting.\"),\n(\"item response theory for language model benchmark evaluation question difficulty\",\"benchmark_context\",\"Gap method-irt-model-background (high): positions EB-IRT against existing IRT-based LLM evaluation. Polo2024EfficientMultiPrompt is already cited, so the query targets IRT-based difficulty modeling beyond it.\"),\n(\"over-fitting in model selection and subsequent selection bias in performance evaluation\",\"core_method\",\"Gap intro-selection-bias-ml-model-selection (high): supports the introduction's claim that the best candidate's score is biased and its interval ignores selection, from the ML model-selection literature. The current bibliography has only statistical and holdout-reuse work plus Efron1997Bootstrap632 and Recht2019ImageNet.\"),\n(\"benchmark test set reuse overfitting meta-analysis repeated evaluation machine learning\",\"result_driven_theme\",\"Gap intro-selection-bias-ml-model-selection (high): empirical evidence for the size of selection-induced optimism after repeated test-set reuse. Recht2019ImageNet is the only such study cited; this adds breadth without a full literature refresh.\"),\n(\"large language models as optimizers automatic prompt optimization\",\"baseline_comparator\",\"Gap related-work-prompt-optimizers (medium): the claim that no prompt-search work gives selection-aware uncertainty rests on DSPy, MIPRO and Shi2024PromptBAI alone. Adds the main LLM-driven prompt optimizers (e.g. APE, OPRO, ProTeGi lineage) as comparators. Covers the evaluation-overfitting-on-small-validation-sets angle where results allow.\"),\n]\nd['queries']=[{\"query\":a,\"category\":b,\"rationale\":c} for a,b,c in q]\nd['central_topic']=d['central_topic']\nd['failure_reason']=\"\"\nd['status']=\"ready\"\njson.dump(d,open('postdraft_reference_query_plan.json','w'),indent=2)\nmd=\"\"\"# Post-draft reference query plan\n\n**Status:** ready. No retrieval was run in this stage.\n\n## Central topic\n%s\n\n## Approach\n`draft_reference_gaps` flags three under-cited places in the current draft. Each gets a small, paragraph-specific query set (6 queries total). Adaptive data analysis, post-selection inference, scoring rules, Qwen2.5 and MMLU-Pro are already cited and are not re-queried.\n\n## Queries\n\n### 1. method-irt-model-background (high, background)\nAnchor: \"each logged outcome follows y_{qk} ~ Bernoulli(sigma(a_k - b_q))\".\nNo IRT or Rasch work is cited, although the reporter is named EB-IRT.\n1. `%s` [core_method]: credits the IRT/Rasch foundations.\n2. `%s` [core_method]: ties the hierarchical-prior and Laplace empirical-Bayes fit to prior IRT estimation work. This is distinct from the existing Efron Tweedie and Stein entries.\n3. `%s` [benchmark_context]: positions EB-IRT against IRT-based LLM evaluation, beyond the already-cited Polo2024EfficientMultiPrompt.\n\n### 2. intro-selection-bias-ml-model-selection (high, positioning)\nAnchor: \"It is therefore a biased estimate of that candidate's accuracy on new questions, and the usual interval around it ignores the selection.\"\nThe ML model-selection literature is missing. Only Efron1997Bootstrap632 and Recht2019ImageNet exist on the ML side.\n4. `%s` [core_method]: supports the central bias claim.\n5. `%s` [result_driven_theme]: empirical evidence of optimism after repeated test-set reuse.\n\n### 3. related-work-prompt-optimizers (medium, comparator)\nAnchor: \"DSPy and MIPRO automate prompt and pipeline optimization\".\n6. `%s` [baseline_comparator]: widens the comparator set beyond DSPy, MIPRO and Shi2024PromptBAI. Evaluation overfitting on small validation sets is covered only if results surface it.\n\n## Out of scope\nGeneric hyperparameter-optimization or AutoML surveys, run chronology, and a broader bibliography rebalance. The forbidden query patterns from `reference_query_plan.json` are carried over.\n\"\"\" % tuple([d['central_topic']]+[x[0] for x in q])\nopen('postdraft_reference_query_plan.md','w').write(md)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;print(len(json.load(open('postdraft_reference_query_plan.json'))['queries']))\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":25748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":876},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"656c76ab-65c2-4296-9c0d-84c67e8d12ff","uuid":"48cb0ea0-b4c1-4c7b-890e-31c449efd510","timestamp":"2026-11-11T14:46:35.512Z","request_id":"req_011CgwKdghqyd2qf3qEjTv2i"}
